<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Cosmin Forest</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1497">1497</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the Cosmin Forest was fought on 26 October 1497 in northern Moldavia, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephen-the-great">Stephen the Great</a> ambushed the retreating army of the Polish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-i-albert">John I Albert</a> after his failed siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suceava">Suceava</a>, ending Polish attempts to control Moldavia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-cosmin-forest.jpg" alt="Battle of the Cosmin Forest" width="320" height="255" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Juliusz Kossak · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cherubin_Gniewosz_in_the_battle_of_Suceava_1497.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1484 Sultan Bayezid II captured Chilia and Cetatea Albă, cutting Moldavia off from the sea, and in 1497 Stephen beat a Polish invasion under John I Albert in the <b>Cosmin Forest</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/principality-of-moldavia">Principality of Moldavia · Military</a></li></ul></section>
